  "notes": "Control Plane resumable verification expanded within the existing 5-point Release Risk Budget to close Template Factory page-level browser replay. Planned release scope is quality-infrastructure + release-infrastructure + storefront-ui (5/5, three subsystems); DOMAIN-BUILDER is included only for the QA catalog page-fingerprint projection. Promotion is engine-identity-bound: any verification engine/policy change falls back to SHADOW and must re-earn promotion. No production runtime/template behavior is changed. Template Factory selective browser replay is implemented as a subordinate evidence checkpoint inside the existing Template Factory Quality Gate; no parallel workflow authority. Merge-readiness stress verification exposed a transient duplicate E13 acceptance root in the Product Owner functional-proof browser session; scope was widened to harden that existing runner with fail-closed cardinality convergence plus regression coverage."
